# Code Quality Standards

## Naming Conventions
- Use PascalCase for classes, methods, and properties
- Use camelCase for local variables and parameters
- Use descriptive names (e.g., `crystalBallMessage` not `msg`)
- Prefix private fields with underscore if needed

## Method Organization
- Keep methods small and focused (single responsibility)
- Use async/await for I/O operations
- Handle exceptions appropriately
- Return meaningful values

## Component Structure
- Place related code together
- Use `@code` blocks for component logic
- Separate UI markup from business logic
- Use dependency injection for services

## Error Handling
- Use try-catch blocks for external API calls
- Return user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for debugging
- Don't expose internal errors to users

## Performance
- Use caching for expensive operations
- Implement proper disposal patterns
- Use `using` statements for disposable resources
- Avoid blocking UI thread

## Example Quality Code:
```csharp
private async Task HandleFileSelected(InputFileChangeEventArgs e)
{
    try
    {
        var file = e.File;
        using var stream = file.OpenReadStream();
        using var reader = new StreamReader(stream);
        var content = await reader.ReadToEndAsync();
        confirmationText = $"File '{file.Name}' uploaded successfully!";
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        confirmationText = "Error uploading file";
        // Log error
    }
}
```